            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0252" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/187</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-10-15T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                                1917, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1775. Your 1821, September 29. Willard replies: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Unable to send at once high railroad officer of kind you request. Stevens
                            is considered one of the ablest railroad engineers in this country. It
                            is suggested that he act as adviser to Minister of Means of
                            Communication in Petrograd, and let Miller look after operations on
                            Trans-Siberian which he is thoroughly competent to do. George Emerson,
                            general manager, Great Northern Railroad, will leave for Vladivostok in
                            about three weeks with force of 300 American railroad officers and
                            skilled mechanics. They will give <pb facs="0253" n="203" xml:id="pg203"
                            /> Miller the support he needs on Trans-Siberian. I recommend above
                            arrangement and feel certain no better selection than Stevens could be
                            made for particular place or duties you have in mind in Petrograd.
                            Advise if this arrangement will be satisfactory.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Department concurs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
